                <pb facs="0577" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg495"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2028.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Saltillo to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Saltillo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-27T13:00:00-06:41"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27, 1911—1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Yesterday the State leader of Coahuila elected Oscar Garza, a banker, provisional
                    governor, but Madero insisted upon election of Carranza, who was chosen this
                    morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Voetter.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
